WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.080
A finance minister
announces some good news:

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.600
the deficit has been cut
for the third year in a row.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.390
The same week, a headline
says the national debt

4
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.070
has hit a new record.

5
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.910
Both statements are true.

6
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.530
So is someone getting the numbers wrong?

7
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.270
If a country's yearly
deficit keeps shrinking,

8
00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.630
how can its debt still be growing?

9
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.360
In this mission, you'll sort
government spending into three kinds,

10
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.400
and work out a budget balance.

11
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.410
Then you'll find out why lenders,

12
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.530
and credit ratings, care so
much about the size of a debt.

13
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.280
Your mission: explain how a
shrinking deficit and a growing

14
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.110
debt can both be true.
